  "accessionCode": "CCX-A-14896",
  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>One and a third metres of dyed cord carrying nine knots with the fourth left loose, weighted at one end with a drilled stone, left in a storm gap of the outer arc and recovered after the claim it answered had been settled. The dye is a deep red taken from ground iron sand and is laid on in a single pass so that its polarisation reads clean, which is the half of the message the weir builders cannot see. The cord is salt-stiffened and one strand is broken near the weighted end. It was handed over in 2274 by the house that tied it, twelve tides after the gap was closed.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
  ],
